    "result_text": "The build is green. The acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` feature for owner registration (`POST /api/owners` \u2192 read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), following the project's OfficeFloor/OpenAPI conventions.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`**\n   - Added optional write field `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added read-only derived field `ageBand` to the `Owner` schema \u2014 an enum of `MINOR` / `ADULT` / `SENIOR`.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date DATE` column) with getter/setter. `ageBand` is *not* stored; it is derived at read time.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Tests run on `hsqldb`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation (wired via `@Mapping`): when `birthDate` is present it computes full years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (falling back to the current date if none is stored) and maps to `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (\u226565); returns `null` when no birth date was supplied, so the field stays absent for backward compatibility.\n\n`birthDate` auto-maps from the request DTO onto the entity via the existing MapStruct `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, so it flows through the create pipeline (`BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner`) and is persisted, then surfaced plus the derived `ageBand` on read. No new pipeline step or controller was needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`GET` responders use the mapper directly.\n\nTest suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1/1 passing.",
