    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the established pattern of this mapper. `OwnerMapper` already holds a family of read-time derived fields, each expressed as a `@Mapping(target=..., expression=\"java(x(owner))\")` pairing with a `default` method (`contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`, `checkDigit`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `locality`). The new `ageBand` follows that convention exactly \u2014 right unit, no duplication, and sitting among peers of comparable complexity (e.g. `checkDigit` is a similarly self-contained inline computation, so keeping `ageBand` inline rather than extracting a helper is consistent).\n\nSupporting pieces are placed where a maintainer would expect: the `birthDate` field + getter/setter on `Owner` mirror the adjacent `registrationDate`, the column is added across all four DB dialect schemas, and the OpenAPI schema documents both the input `birthDate` and the read-only derived `ageBand`. The null-handling and \"compute against registrationDate, fall back to now\" behavior matches the spec and is documented in the Javadoc in the same voice as the surrounding methods.\n\nMinor, non-blocking: the body uses fully-qualified `java.time.LocalDate`/`java.time.Period` instead of imports. Imports would read slightly cleaner, but there's existing precedent for in-body FQNs (`locality` references `OwnerCustomerCode` fully-qualified), so this stays within the file's conventions and isn't worth a change request.",
